###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#BroadleavedTree
:BroadleavedTree rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf :Tree ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy "Wikipedia" ;
                 rdfs:label "Laubbaum"@de ,
                            "broadleaved tree"@en ;
                 skos:definition "A broad-leaved tree is any tree within the diverse botanical group of angiosperms that has flat leaves and produces seeds inside of fruits."@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Classification
:Classification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty :classifies ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing
                                    ] ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :Quality ;
                dcterms:description """The classification is  dependent on some quality not directly measured, but assesed 
by the inventory team. Thus a classification can be interpreted as a quality for which the value space has been partitioned into several subsets of the correspondent value
space. The classification then notes in which subset the entity falls. As the classification fixes its own \"datatype\",  there is no need for metadata, so for the sake of conciseness the enitity is directly related to the classification instance.

A concrete classification is a subclass of  this class. The different subsets of the values space are modeled as instances and singleton subclasses of the classification class. This allows for grouping  several subclasses. 

An entity is related to a classification instance by a subproperty of the  the object property  `is_classified_as`.  The inverse property is called `is_classification_of`"""@en ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                rdfs:label "Klassifizierung"@de ;
                skos:definition <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ,
                                "A classification of an entity is a partition of some superclass into subclasses, which is not modeled as DL Concepts (OWL classes) but as a quality having the subclasses as a discrete value space."@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "clasificación"@es ,
                               "classification"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ClusterAreaSet
:ClusterAreaSet rdf:type owl:Class ;
                owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty :implements ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom :TemplateCluster
                                    ] ;
                rdfs:subClassOf geo:Feature ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty :hasReferencePosition ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom :Position
                                ] ;
                skos:definition "Set of plot main areas, which implement the templats plote a template cluster implies.  Has a central posiition that is sufficiently close to the implemented template cluster's  scheduled position"@en ;
                skos:note """The Spanish IFN doesn't use clusters, hence there always is a cluster area set derived from the single plot main area it contains.

The German BWI does not model this class and only knows template clusters, hence every template cluster gets a standard cluster area set. Its reference position always 
equals the  template cluster's originally scheduled position. 

The US FIA models only cluster area sets (calling them \"plot\") and the template clusters are implied in  their data. 

There is the event that a field crew does not identify the cluster area set's reference position of the previous inventory cycle and sets a new reference position. This ends the lifetime of a cluster area set and  a newly created  implements the corresponding template cluster. 

With the German BWI this event is handled at the plot main area level only and handled there,  in cannot happen to a cluster area set.

For the US FIA the cluster area set is the main class dealing with the event and propagates it to the plot main areas it contains."""@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "Cluster-Gebietsmenge"@de ,
                               "cluster area set"@en ,
                               "conjunto de areás de un  acopiamiento"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ClusterAreaSetClassification
:ClusterAreaSetClassification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                              owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty :classifies ;
                                                    owl:someValuesFrom :ClusterAreaSet
                                                  ] ;
                              rdfs:subClassOf :Classification ;
                              skos:prefLabel "Klassifikation einer Cluster-Gebietsmenge"@de ,
                                             "clasificación de un conjunto de areás de un acopiamiento"@es ,
                                             "classification of a cluster area set"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ClusterAreaSetSamplingStatus
:ClusterAreaSetSamplingStatus rdf:type owl:Class ;
                              rdfs:subClassOf :ClusterAreaSetClassification ;
                              skos:definition "classification of a cluster area set according to if it is sampled or not and if not states why."@en ;
                              skos:prefLabel "Erfassungsstatus einer Cluster-Gebietsmenge"@de ,
                                             "cluster area set sampling status"@en ,
                                             "estado de muestreo de un conjunto de areás de acopiamiento"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ClusterDataset
:ClusterDataset rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :DataCollection ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty :contains ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom :PlotDataset
                                ] ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty :isPartOf ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom :NationalForestInventory
                                ] ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                skos:altLabel "Datensatz zu einem Trakt (BWI)"@de ,
                              "dataset for a plot (FIA)"@en ;
                skos:definition "data collected by a fieldcrew at for cluster"@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "Cluster-Datensatz"@de ,
                               "cluster dataset"@en ,
                               "datos de acopiamiento"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Conifer
:Conifer rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf :Tree ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy "Wikipedia, crossnfi"@en ;
         rdfs:label "Nadelbaum"@de ,
                    "conifer"@en ;
         skos:definition "Conifers are primarily perennial, woody trees, mostly evergreen and mostly with needle shaped leaves,  having a regular branching pattern, reproducing with male and female cones, usually on the same tree."@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#DBH
:DBH rdf:type owl:Class ;
     rdfs:subClassOf :Quantity ;
     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
     rdfs:seeAlso "Tomppo E et al 2010, National Forest Inventories: Pathways for Common Reporting, Appendix" ;
     skos:definition "The breast height of a tree is located at 1.3 m from the base point of the axis of the stem."@en ;
     skos:note """Instances are related by ´qudt:hasUnit' to a ´qudt:Unit´, which ´qudt:hasQuantityKind´ ´qudt:Length´. This usually is ´unit:M´, ´unit:CM´, ´unit:FT´, ´unit:YD´ or ´unit:IN´. 

Tomppo et al base point: On level terrain the base point is the point resulting from the intersection  of the stem axis and the ground surface. On sloped terrain and on inclined trees the identification of the base point requires the previous identification of an  an intersection point. This intersection point is the highest point on the cross sectional  area that results from the intersection of the ground surface with the stem. A line through the intersection point and perpendicular to the stem axis yields the base point in these  cases.""" ;
     skos:prefLabel "Brusthöhendurchmesser (BHD)"@de ,
                    "diameter at breast height (DBH)"@en ,
                    "diámetro a la altura de pecho (DAP)"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#DRC
:DRC rdf:type owl:Class ;
     rdfs:subClassOf :Quantity ;
     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
     rdfs:seeAlso "USDA Forest Service, 2023, Forest Inventory and Analysis Glossary" ;
     skos:definition "The diameter of a tree stem(s) measured at root collar or at the point nearest the ground line (whichever is higher) that represents the basal area of the tree, measured outside the bark."@en ;
     skos:note """Instances are related by ´qudt:hasUnit' to a ´qudt:Unit´, which ´qudt:hasQuantityKind´ ´qudt:Length´. This usually is ´unit:M´, ´unit:CM´, ´unit:FT´, ´unit:YD´ or ´unit:IN´. 

FIA:
For multi-stemmed trees, d.r.c. is calculated from an equation that incorporates the individual stem diameter measurements. The point of diameter measurement may vary for woodland trees with stems that are abnormally formed. With the exception of seedlings, woodland stems qualifying for measurement must be at least 1.0 inch in diameter or larger and at least 1.0 foot in length"""@en ;
     skos:prefLabel "Wurzelhalsdurchmesser"@en ,
                    "diameter at root collar"@en ,
                    "diámetro del cuello del raíz"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#DataCollection
:DataCollection rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty :inYear ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer
                                ] ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                skos:broader "bfo : generally dependent continuant (31)"@en ;
                skos:definition "a collection of data"@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "Datensammlung"@de ,
                               "colleción de datos"@es ,
                               "data collection"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Developed
:Developed rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf :LandUse ;
           skos:definition "area which is altered for everyday human use"@en ;
           skos:note "urban areas, traffic ways, mining, recreational (eg golf courses)"@de ;
           skos:prefLabel "Siedlungsfläche"@de ,
                          "developed area"@en ,
                          "uso artificial"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Distance
:Distance rdf:type owl:Class ;
          rdfs:subClassOf :Quantity ;
          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
          rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance> ;
          skos:definition "The length of a straight line between two points"@en ;
          skos:note "instances are related by ´qudt:hasUnit' to a ´qudt:Unit´, which ´qudt:hasQuantityKind´ ´qudt:Length´. This usually is ´unit:M´, ´unit:CM´, ´unit:FT´, ´unit:YD´ or ´unit:IN´." ;
          skos:prefLabel "Entfernung"@de ,
                         "distance"@en ,
                         "distancia"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#FixedCircleSample
:FixedCircleSample rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :SampleOfTreesOfMinDiameter ;
                   rdfs:label "FixedCircleSample"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ForestArea
:ForestArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ,
                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                              owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                              owl:someValuesFrom :InventoryArea
                            ] ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ,
                             "FAO  Forest Resource Assement - Terms and Definitions"@en ;
            rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.fao.org/forest-resources-assessment/en/> ;
            skos:definition """The part of an total area on which forest vegetation is stocking. The definition for forest vegetation are specific to the NFI. Expanding the FAO reference definition for forest gives:

Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. Includes area whose vegetation currently doesn't satisfy these conditions, but did so in the past and is expected to do so in the future."""@en ;
            skos:note """The criteria for the single NFIs: 
German BWI:  forest trees stocking on an area of at least 0.1 ha with a minimum width of 10 m and stocking on at least 50 % of that area. 

US FIA:  forest trees stocking on an area of at least 1 acre  (~0.4 ha) with a minimum width of 120 feet (36.6 m) and stocking on  or covering at least 10 % of that area.

Spanish IFN:  forest trees stocking on an area of which they cover at least 10 %.

Further notes: 
US FIA also includes chapparal and pinyon-juniper formations, which are excluded by the international definition (and also in Spain). 

German non-stocked forest area is excluded, although it would partly be included in the FAO definition."""@en ;
            skos:prefLabel "Waldfläche"@de ,
                           "area de bosque"@es ,
                           "forest area"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ForestPlotSubarea
:ForestPlotSubarea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :PlotSubArea ,
                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                     owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                                     owl:someValuesFrom :ForestArea
                                   ] ,
                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                     owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                                     owl:someValuesFrom :InventoryArea
                                   ] ;
                   skos:definition """intersection of the immediate surroundings of a plot with the total forest area of the
total area the plot is contained in. Thus its vegetation usually is forest vegetation"""@en ;
                   skos:prefLabel "Wald-Plotteilfläche"@de ,
                                  "forest plot subarea"@en ,
                                  "área de parcela en bosque"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#GrowthRegion
:GrowthRegion rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
              skos:prefLabel "Wuchsgebiet"@de ,
                             "growth region"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Herb
:Herb rdf:type owl:Class ;
      rdfs:subClassOf :Plant ;
      rdfs:isDefinedBy "Wikipedia"@en ;
      skos:prefLabel "herbaceous plant"@en ,
                     "hierba"@es ,
                     "krautige Pflanze"@de .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#HumanActivity
:HumanActivity rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf :Process ;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
               skos:definition "a process where the main actors are human"@en ;
               skos:prefLabel "actuación humana"@es ,
                              "human activity"@en ,
                              "menschliche Aktitvität"@de .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#InvalidCluster
:InvalidCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :NonSampledCluster ;
                skos:definition "all the cluster area set's  plot main  area are not valid"@en ,
                                "inválido"@es ;
                skos:note """possible reasons are
- all the cluster is in non-inventory area 
- its at the location of a previous inventory instance, but was dropped in this instance for example because the cluster / plot density was dropped"""@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "invalid"@en ,
                               "ungültig"@de .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#InvalidPlot
:InvalidPlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :NonsampledPlot ;
             skos:definition "the plot area is not valid"@en ;
             skos:note """possible reasons are
- its hypothetical location corresponds to the pattern of a cluster or grid, but is situated in non-inventory area or an area with a different sampling density. 
- its at the location of a previous inventory instance, but was dropped in this instance for example because the cluster / plot density was dropped"""@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "invalid"@en ,
                            "inválido"@es ,
                            "ungültig"@de .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#InventoryArea
:InventoryArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
               skos:definition "part of the earth surface in which a National Forest Inventory is applied. Most often coincides with the countrie's state area."@en ;
               skos:prefLabel "Inventurgebiet"@de ,
                              "inventory area"@en ,
                              "área de inventario"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#InventoryScheme
:InventoryScheme rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 skos:broader "bfo : generally dependent continuant (31)"@en ;
                 skos:definition "the design and planning of an inventory project or a part of it"@en ;
                 skos:prefLabel "Inventurentwurf"@de ,
                                "esquema de inventorio"@es ,
                                "inventory scheme"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#LandUse
:LandUse rdf:type owl:Class ;
         owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                               owl:onProperty :isLandUseOf ;
                               owl:someValuesFrom :PlotSubArea
                             ] ;
         rdfs:subClassOf :PlotSubareaClassification ;
         skos:definition "classification of a nonforest plot subarea by its land use"@en ;
         skos:prefLabel <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ,
                        "Landnutzung"@de ,
                        "land use"@en ,
                        "uso del suelo"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#MapSubarea
:MapSubarea rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
            skos:definition "a subarea delineated in a map, most often a polygon or multipolygon. It has an area (quantity)."@en ,
                            "subárea de una mapa"@es ;
            skos:prefLabel "Karten-Teilfläche"@de ,
                           "map subarea"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#MunicipalOwner
:MunicipalOwner rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :OwnerGroup ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                skos:definition "an area owned by a municipality" ;
                skos:prefLabel "kommunaler Eigentümer"@de ,
                               "municipal owner"@en ,
                               "propietario municipal"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Municipality
:Municipality rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
              rdfs:seeAlso <https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/local-administrative-units> ;
              skos:definition "a administrative division of smallest level, often having corporate status and powers of self-government or jurisdiction"@en ;
              skos:prefLabel "Kommune"@de ,
                             "municipality"@en ,
                             "municipio"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NUTS1Region
:NUTS1Region rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             rdfs:seeAlso <https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts> ;
             skos:altLabel "Region auf NUTS Ebene 1"@de ,
                           "region of NUTS level 1"@en ;
             skos:note """Nomenclature of territorial units for statistics (Nomenclature des Unités territoriales statistiques)

US states  are often too large for the EU criteria and alternatively could be filed under NUTS level 0 pi
Spains level 1 seem to be artificial groupings of level 2 autonomous communities"""@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Land"@de ,
                            "major socio-economic regions"@en ,
                            "región de nivel de NUTS de 1"@es ,
                            "state"@en-us .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NUTS2Region
:NUTS2Region rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             rdfs:seeAlso <https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts> ;
             skos:altLabel "Region auf NUTS Level 2"@de ,
                           "región de nivel de NUTS de 2"@es ;
             skos:definition "basic regions (for regional policies)"@en ;
             skos:note """Nomenclature of territorial units for statistics (Nomenclature des Unités territoriales statistiques)

US FIA uses unit,  a grouping of counties which is only valid FIA internally.

In Germany often identical with NUTS1."""@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Bezirk"@de ,
                            "comunidad autónoma"@en ,
                            "region of NUTS level 2"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NUTS3Region
:NUTS3Region rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             rdfs:seeAlso <https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts> ;
             skos:altLabel "Region auf NUTS Level 2"@de ,
                           "region of NUTS level 3"@en ,
                           "región de nivel de NUTS de 3"@es ;
             skos:definition "small regions (for specific diagnoses)"@de ;
             skos:note "Nomenclature of territorial units for statistics (Nomenclature des Unités territoriales statistiques)"@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Kreis"@de ,
                            "county"@en-us ,
                            "provincia"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NationalForestInventory
:NationalForestInventory rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf :DataCollection ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty :collectedOnArea ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom :InventoryArea
                                         ] ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty :contains ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom :PlotDataset
                                         ] ;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                         skos:broader "bfo : generally dependent continuant (31)"@en ;
                         skos:definition "A collection of data and metadata of measurements in forests which are collected in a  a National Forest Inventory Project."@en ;
                         skos:prefLabel "National Forest Inventory"@en ,
                                        "Nationale Forstinventur"@de ,
                                        "inventario forestal nacional"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NonForestArea
:NonForestArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ,
                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                 owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                                 owl:someValuesFrom :InventoryArea
                               ] ;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
               skos:definition "area in an inventory area that is not forest area"@en ;
               skos:prefLabel "Nichtwaldfläche"@de ,
                              "non forest area"@en ,
                              "área de no bosque"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NonForestPlotSubarea
:NonForestPlotSubarea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf :PlotSubArea ,
                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                        owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                                        owl:someValuesFrom :InventoryArea
                                      ] ;
                      skos:definition "a plot subarea which is not located in forest area"@en ;
                      skos:prefLabel "Nichtwald-Plotunterfläche"@de ,
                                     "non forest plot subarea"@en ,
                                     "subárea de parcela de no bosque"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NonInventoryArea
:NonInventoryArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                  skos:prefLabel "Nichtinventurgebiet"@de ,
                                 "non-inventory area"@en ,
                                 "part of the earth surface which is not inventory area for a certain NFI"@en ,
                                 "área de non-inventario"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NonSampledCluster
:NonSampledCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :ClusterAreaSetSamplingStatus ;
                   skos:definition "a cluster area set, which contains no plot main area which was sampled"@en ,
                                   "nicht erfasst"@de ,
                                   "no muestrada"@es ,
                                   "nonsampled"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NonsampledOnlyNonForest
:NonsampledOnlyNonForest rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf :NonSampledCluster ;
                         skos:definition "a cluster area set which was not sampled as it was obvious beforehand that it contained only non-forest"@en ;
                         skos:prefLabel "nur Nicht-Wald"@de ,
                                        "only non forest"@en ,
                                        "solo no bosque"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NonsampledPlot
:NonsampledPlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :PlotMainAreaSamplingStatus ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                skos:definition "a plot subarea which was not sampled"@en ;
                skos:note "this includes plot main areas that fall under the umbrella of \"other reason\" classifications"@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "nicht erfasst"@de ,
                               "no muestrada"@es ,
                               "non-sampled"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NotAccessibleCluster
:NotAccessibleCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf :NonSampledCluster ;
                      skos:definition "a cluster area set which was not sampled by all its plots not being accessible."@en ,
                                      "nicht betretbar"@de ,
                                      "no accesible"@es ,
                                      "not accessible"@en ;
                      skos:note "the reason can be difficult terrain, a temporary hazardous situation (storm throw or insect damage) or   legal access restriction of public (military) or private nature"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#NotAccessiblePlot
:NotAccessiblePlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :NonsampledPlot ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                   skos:definition "a plot main area which was not sampled by the plot not being accessible."@en ;
                   skos:note "the reason can be difficult terrain, a temporary hazardous situation (storm throw or insect damage) or   legal access restriction of public (military) or private nature"@en ;
                   skos:prefLabel "nicht betretbar"@de ,
                                  "no accesible"@es ,
                                  "not accessible"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#OrganizationallyImpossibleCluster
:OrganizationallyImpossibleCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf :NonSampledCluster ;
                                   skos:definition "a cluster area set  which was not sampled for organizational reasons"@en ;
                                   skos:note "Possible reasons are lack of time in in a fixed timeslot,  loss of data, rescheduling for a later sampling"@en ;
                                   skos:prefLabel "imposible organizadormente"@es ,
                                                  "organisatorisch unmöglich"@de ,
                                                  "organizationally impossible"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#OrganizationallyImpossiblePlot
:OrganizationallyImpossiblePlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf :NonsampledPlot ;
                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                                skos:definition "a plot main area which was not sampled for organizational reasons"@en ;
                                skos:prefLabel "imposiple organizadormente"@es ,
                                               "organisatorisch unmöglich"@de ,
                                               "organizationally impossible"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#OwnerGroup
:OwnerGroup rdf:type owl:Class ;
            owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty :isOwnerGroupOf ;
                                  owl:someValuesFrom :PlotSubArea
                                ] ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :PlotSubareaClassification ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
            skos:definition "classification of a plot subarea by the nature oft its owner according to private or public law" ;
            skos:prefLabel "Eigentümergruppe"@de ,
                           "grupo de propietario"@es ,
                           "owner group"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PermanentlyNonStockedForest
:PermanentlyNonStockedForest rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf :LandUse ;
                             skos:definition """Area, which is permanently not covered by trees for diverging
reasons but closely related to the forest. 

\"Non-Stocked Forest Areas are forest roads, aisles and protection bands with at least 5m width, timber storage places, non-commercial nursery gardens in entanglement
with the forest, temporary seedling collection sites, wildlife meadows and wildlife fields, courts and buildings serving forestry use, recreation sites connected to the forest, as well as rocks, stone runs, gravel sites and water bodies located in the forest. Also marshlands and bogs located in the forest are considered Non-Stocked
Forest Area.\"

Riedel T., Hennig P., Polley H., Schwitzgebel F.,  2021, 
Aufnahmeanweisung für die vierte Bundeswaldinventur (2021 - 2022),  
BMEL Bundesministerium für Ernährung und Landwirtschaft, Bonn"""@en ;
                             skos:note """A land category in countries with a German forestry tradition. Counts as forest area in Germany, but is not used for calculating statistics. Other NFIs map these areas partly as forest, partly as non-forest. 

Not to be confused with temporarily unstocked forest area, which is counted here 
as forest area.

In the Spanish IFN there is a sub-category of temporarily unstocked forest area (internal to the Spanish hierarchy) called \"complements to the forest\", (complementos del bosque) with the single example of firebreaks (contrafuegos).

The US FIA either includes them in the forest if they don't meet the relevant size criterie or  breaks up these areas into the corresponding land uses (Developed, Rangeland, _), where several cases like forest roads, power lines or recreational areas are exempted from the minimum size obligations"""@en ;
                             skos:prefLabel "Nichtholzboden"@de ,
                                            "complementos del bosque"@es ,
                                            "permanently non-stocked forest area"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Plant
:Plant rdf:type owl:Class ;
       rdfs:isDefinedBy "Wikipedia"@en ;
       skos:broader "bfo : object (30)" ;
       skos:definition "Plants are the eukaryotic organisms that constitute the kingdom Plantae."@en ;
       skos:prefLabel "Pflanze"@de ,
                      "plant"@en ,
                      "planta"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotAbioticProcess
:PlotAbioticProcess rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf :AbioticProcess ;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                    skos:definition "abiotic process which takes place in a plot subarea"@en ;
                    skos:prefLabel "abiotic process on a plot subarea"@en ,
                                   "abiotischer Prozess auf einer Plotunterfläche"@de ,
                                   "proceso abiótico en a subárea de parcela"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotArea
:PlotArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
          rdfs:subClassOf :Region ;
          dcterms:description "In the population-sample pattern applied for areas this is a sample."@en ;
          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
          skos:broader "bfo : two-dimensional spatial region (9)"@en ;
          skos:definition "The part of the earth surface that is used for classifications and measurements belonging to a plot of a National Forest Inventory"@en ;
          skos:prefLabel "Plotfläche"@de ,
                         "plot area"@en ,
                         "área de  parcela"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotBioticProcess
:PlotBioticProcess rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :BioticProcess ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                   skos:definition "biotic process taking place on a inventory plot subarea"@en ;
                   skos:prefLabel "biotic process on a plot subarea"@en ,
                                  "biotischer Prozess auf einer Plotunterfläche"@de ,
                                  "proceso biótico en una subárea de parcela"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotDataset
:PlotDataset rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :DataCollection ,
                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                               owl:onProperty :isPartOf ;
                               owl:someValuesFrom :NationalForestInventory
                             ] ;
             dcterms:description "The entities that a plot refers to usually are the plot area and the terrain it encompasses, the forest community, human activities taking place on the plot terrain, samples of trees and  deadwood taken on the plot area."@en ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             skos:altLabel "Datensatz zu einer Traktecke (BWI)"@de ,
                           "dataset for a subplot (FIA)"@en ;
             skos:definition "A collection of data recorded in a National Forest Inventory of entities that are located in the neighbourhood of a reference location. Refers to this location by `hasCentralPoint`"@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Plot-Daten"@de ,
                            "datos de parcela"@es ,
                            "plot dataset"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotDensityArea
:PlotDensityArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ,
                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                   owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                                   owl:someValuesFrom :InventoryArea
                                 ] ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                 skos:definition "An area where plots or clusters are spatially arranged by an algorithm resulting in a certain density of plots and clusters."@en ;
                 skos:note "a set of areas with uniform plot entities partitions an inventory area"@en ;
                 skos:prefLabel "Gebiet mit einheitlicher Stichprobendichte"@de ,
                                "area of uniform plot density"@en ,
                                "área de densidad de parcela uniforma"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotForestVegetationClassification
:PlotForestVegetationClassification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty :classifies ;
                                                          owl:someValuesFrom :Vegetation
                                                        ] ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf :Classification ;
                                    skos:prefLabel "Klassifikation einer Wald-Vegetation"@de ,
                                                   "clasificación de una vegetación del bosque"@es ,
                                                   "classification of a forest vegetation"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotGreaterArea
:PlotGreaterArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf :PlotArea ;
                 dcterms:description """This class is intended not to be populated with instances. 

Any plot subarea is contained in a single plot greater area, which will not be found in 
the data and is kept here just for conceptually clarity. 

For some classifications or even measurements a wider area then the dilineated one is used, eg for classifying the macroterrain one needs to consider an area that is well beyond any defined limits. Else how could one differentiate between upper slope and lower slope.  For some classifications a concrete area is given, eg the BWI states that forest type has to be assesed in a 25m radius around the plot central point. 

When these classifications are taken from entities found in the greater plot area, they are copied over to the plot subareas. That is each contained plot subarea or entity related to one of the subplot areas gets classified. 

As an example take the above assesment of  forest type in BWI where there are 2 stands delineated.  The  classification is on the Forest Community, which is located in the plot greater area and thus in both plot-subareas. Thus each plot subarea refers to the same forest type entity and its classification, but the properties are settled in the plot subareas. There is not an instance of the plot greater area, so it cannot be refered to."""@en ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                 skos:definition "Area around the plot that is not delineated, but still used for assessing classifications."@en ;
                 skos:prefLabel "erweiterte Plotfläche"@de ,
                                "plot greater area"@en ,
                                "área ampliada de parcela"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotHumanActivity
:PlotHumanActivity rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :HumanActivity ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                   skos:definition "human activity that takes place on an inventory plot subarea"@en ;
                   skos:prefLabel "actividad humana en una subárea de parcela"@es ,
                                  "human activity on a plot subarea"@en ,
                                  "menschliche Aktivität auf einer Plotunterfläche"@de .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotMainArea
:PlotMainArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
              owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty :implements ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom :TemplatePlot
                                  ] ;
              rdfs:subClassOf :PlotArea ,
                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                owl:onProperty geo:sfContains ;
                                owl:someValuesFrom :PlotSubArea
                              ] ;
              skos:altLabel "immediate surroundings"@en ;
              skos:definition """An area around the plot reference position, which itself in combination with entities located on it is assessed by the field crew.  Its identity is defined by its central point. 
It implements a template plot by its central point being sufficiently close to  the template plot's scheduled position.

Generally there is no explicit definition, but it generally is the circle area of radius between 18 and 25 m m around the plot central position."""@en ;
              skos:prefLabel "Plot-Hauptgebiet"@de ,
                             "plot main area"@en ,
                             "área principal de parcela"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotMainAreaClassification
:PlotMainAreaClassification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            rdfs:subClassOf :Classification ;
                            skos:prefLabel "Klassifikation eines Plot-Hauptgebietes"@de ,
                                           "clasificación de una areá principal de parcela"@es ,
                                           "plot main area classification"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotMainAreaSamplingStatus
:PlotMainAreaSamplingStatus rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty :isPlotSamplingStatusOf ;
                                                  owl:someValuesFrom :PlotMainArea
                                                ] ;
                            rdfs:subClassOf :PlotMainAreaClassification ;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                            skos:definition "classification of a plot main area on if it was sampled or not. If negative also gives the reason."@en ;
                            skos:prefLabel "Erfassungszustand einer Plot-Hauptfläche"@de ,
                                           "estado de muestreo de un areá principal de parcela"@es ,
                                           "sampling status of a plot main area"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotSubArea
:PlotSubArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :PlotArea ,
                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                               owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                               owl:someValuesFrom :PlotMainArea
                             ] ,
                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                               owl:onProperty :describedByPlot ;
                               owl:someValuesFrom :PlotDataset
                             ] ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             skos:altLabel "condition class (FIA)"@en ;
             skos:definition "A part of the plot greater area for which boundaries are established to other parts and which is differentiated from these other parts by criteria specific to the National Forest Inventory, most often at least based on a Forest / Nonforest distinction."@en ;
             skos:note """Classifications of Terrain, Area, Forest Community and Human Activity are spatially applied at this level, which means either the area directly or an entity located in it is classified. 

Classifications which are true for all the plot area this plot subarea is part of are repeated for every plot subarea of the parent plot area. 

Classifications of terrain and legal status are applied directly to the area with their 
different ontological entities being short-circuited into this class for the sake of brevity. 

Possible boundaries are refered to by `geo:hasGeometry`

If a National Forest Inventory divides a plot greater area into subareas that have a finer type system than crossnfi, then different plot subareas of same crossnfi-class are created, with differing classifications in the differentiation quality. Eg FIA divides its condition classes also along owner group, while crossnfi only knows Forest and Non-Forest. Thus the plot will have several subplot areas of type Forest, which have differing owner group classifications.

FIA is the only NFI of the three which constructs these expliicitly. IFN (Inventario Forestal Nacional) moves the plot if sample areas would fall into Non-Forest or a land use different to the land use of the plot central point and thus avoids the problem. BWI notes boundaries between Forest and Non-Forest and Stands, but uses these boundaries for a mirroring algorithm for its angle count sample, so that the non-forest subplot areas are included into the forest inventory only implicitly by  extending the measurements by fictious entities creating an imaginary world without the forest or stand border."""@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Plotteilfläche"@de ,
                            "plot subarea"@en ,
                            "subárea de parcela"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotSubareaClassification
:PlotSubareaClassification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                           owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty :classifies ;
                                                 owl:someValuesFrom :PlotSubArea
                                               ] ;
                           rdfs:subClassOf :Classification ;
                           skos:definition "a classification where the classified entity is a subplot area or its associated terrain or legal status" ;
                           skos:prefLabel "Klassifikation einer Plotteilfläche"@de ,
                                          "clasificación de una área inferior de parcela"@es ,
                                          "classification of a plot subarea"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotSubareaForestVegetation
:PlotSubareaForestVegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf :PlotSubareaVegetation ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                                               owl:someValuesFrom :ForestPlotSubarea
                                             ] ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty :isPartOf ;
                                               owl:someValuesFrom :TotalAreaForestVegetation
                                             ] ;
                             skos:definition "forest vegetation found on a plot subarea"@en ;
                             skos:prefLabel "Vegetation einer Wald-Plotteilfläche"@de ,
                                            "vegetation de una subparcela en bosque"@es ,
                                            "vegetation of a forest plot subarea"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotSubareaTemporaryNonForestVegetation
:PlotSubareaTemporaryNonForestVegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf :PlotSubareaForestVegetation ;
                                         skos:definition """vegetation arrived at by intersecting the area a total area temporary non-forest vegetation stocks with the immediate surroundings of a plot.

Thus it does not meet the criteria for forest vegetation, but did so in the past and is expected to do so in the future""" ;
                                         skos:prefLabel "vegetación de una subparcela de monte arbolada temporalmente sin cobertura"@es ,
                                                        "vegetation on a temporary non-stocked forest plot subarea"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PlotSubareaVegetation
:PlotSubareaVegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                       rdfs:subClassOf :Vegetation ;
                       skos:definition "the community of plants found on  a  plot subarea"@en ;
                       skos:prefLabel "Vegetation einer Plotteilfläche"@de ,
                                      "vegetación  de un subárea de parcela"@es ,
                                      "vegetation of a plot subarea"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Position
:Position rdf:type owl:Class ;
          rdfs:subClassOf geo:Geometry ;
          skos:note "a point on the earth surface"@en ;
          skos:prefLabel "Position"@de ,
                         "posición"@es ,
                         "position"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#PrivateOwner
:PrivateOwner rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf :OwnerGroup ;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
              skos:definition "an area owned by a private natural or legal person"@en ;
              skos:prefLabel "private owner"@en ,
                             "privater Eigentümer"@de ,
                             "propietario privado"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Process
:Process rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty :takesPlaceIn ;
                           owl:someValuesFrom :Region
                         ] ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
         skos:broader "bfo : process (15)"@en ;
         skos:definition "a process is an entity unfolding in time, taking place in an area and affecting the entities on it"@en ;
         skos:prefLabel "Prozess"@de ,
                        "proceso"@es ,
                        "process"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Quality
:Quality rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty :inYear ;
                           owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer
                         ] ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
         skos:broader "bfo : specifically dependent continuant (20)"@en ;
         skos:closeMatch "bfo : quality (19)"@en ;
         skos:definition "A combination of a quality inherent in a continuant and its value either as a measurement or a categorization"@en ;
         skos:prefLabel "Qualität"@de ,
                        "calidad"@es ,
                        "quality"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Quantity
:Quantity rdf:type owl:Class ;
          rdfs:subClassOf qudt:Quantity ,
                          :Quality ;
          dcterms:description ""@en ;
          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
          skos:definition "A quality that refers to a numerical value by a subproperty of `qudt:value` and its metadata like physical units by `qudt:hasUnit`"@en ;
          skos:prefLabel "Quantität"@de ,
                         "cantidad"@es ,
                         "quantity"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Rangelands
:Rangelands rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :LandUse ;
            skos:altLabel "monte desarbolado (sin humedales) y monte desarbolado con arbolado disperso"@es ;
            skos:definition "Weideland"@de ,
                            "land with vegetation suited for grazing"@en ,
                            "pasto"@es ;
            skos:prefLabel "rangelands"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ReferencePositionRelocatedCluster
:ReferencePositionRelocatedCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf :NonSampledCluster ;
                                   skos:definition "Referenzposition verlegt"@de ,
                                                   "reference position relocated"@en ,
                                                   "the field crew relocated the reference position of the cluster area set, creating a new cluster area set as replacement"@en ;
                                   skos:note "Either the field crew was unable to identify the cluster area set's reference point.or the position was outside the tolerance distance of the scheduled point."@en ;
                                   skos:prefLabel "posición de referencia reubicado"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#ReferencePositionRelocatedPlot
:ReferencePositionRelocatedPlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf :NonsampledPlot ;
                                skos:note "Either the field crew was unable to identify the plot main areas's reference point or the position was outside the tolerance distance of the scheduled point."@en ;
                                skos:prefLabel "Referenzposition verlegt"@de ,
                                               "posición de referencia reubicado"@es ,
                                               "reference position relocated"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Region
:Region rdf:type owl:Class ;
        rdfs:subClassOf geo:Feature ,
                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                          owl:onProperty :desrcibedBy ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom :NationalForestInventory
                        ] ,
                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                          owl:onProperty :inYear ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer
                        ] ;
        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
        skos:closeMatch "bfo : two-dimensional spatial region (9)"@en ;
        skos:definition "part of the earth surface interpreted as 2-d"@en ;
        skos:note "In colloquial speech area can also have the same meaning as region. In the compound terms like 'forest area' and similar it has this meaning and these terms are established.  A compound term like 'forest region' would imply a different meaning in colloquial language than intended"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel "Gebiet"@de ,
                       "region"@en ,
                       "región"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Sample
:Sample rdf:type owl:Class ;
        rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                          owl:onProperty :collectedOnArea ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom :SampleArea
                        ] ,
                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                          owl:onProperty :describedByPlot ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom :PlotDataset
                        ] ,
                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                          owl:onProperty :isPartOf ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom :PlotSubareaVegetation
                        ] ,
                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                          owl:onProperty :inYear ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer
                        ] ;
        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
        skos:broader <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ,
                     "bfo : object aggregate (27)"@en ;
        skos:definition "A collection of entities which is chosen for measurements or data recordings. It is  a subset of a larger collection of entities (population)."@en ;
        skos:prefLabel "Probe"@de ,
                       "muestra"@es ,
                       "sample"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampleArea
:SampleArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :PlotArea ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
            skos:altLabel "subplot area (FIA)"@en ;
            skos:definition "A part of a plot subarea on which the entities are located which a sample uses for measurements or data recordings."@en ;
            skos:prefLabel "Probefläche"@de ,
                           "sample area"@en ,
                           "área de muestra"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampleOfTreesBelowMinDiameter
:SampleOfTreesBelowMinDiameter rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf :Sample ;
                               skos:prefLabel "sample of trees below minimum diameter"@en ,
                                              "Probe von Bäumen unter dem Mindestdurchmesser" .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampleOfTreesOfMinDiameter
:SampleOfTreesOfMinDiameter rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            rdfs:subClassOf :Sample ;
                            skos:definition "sample of trees, whose DBH surpasses a minimal requirement"@en ;
                            skos:prefLabel "Probe von Bäumen über dem Mindestdurchmesser"@de ,
                                           "muestra de árboles encima del diámetro minimal"@es ,
                                           "sample of trees of minimum diameter"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampledCluster
:SampledCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :ClusterAreaSetSamplingStatus ;
                skos:definition "a cluster area set which contains  at least one plot main area which was sampled"@en ,
                                "sampled" ;
                skos:prefLabel "aufgenommen"@de ,
                               "muestreada"@es ,
                               "" .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampledOnlyNonforest
:SampledOnlyNonforest rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf :SampledCluster ;
                      skos:definition "the cluster area set contains only plot main areas without a forest plot subarea. At least one plot main area was sampled."@en ;
                      skos:prefLabel "aufgenommen nur Nicht-Wald"@de ,
                                     "muestreada solo non bosque"@es ,
                                     "sampled only nonforest" .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampledPlot
:SampledPlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :PlotMainAreaSamplingStatus ,
                             :SamplingStatus ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             skos:definition "a plot main area, that was sampled"@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "erfasst"@de ,
                            "muestrada"@es ,
                            "sampled"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SampledWithForest
:SampledWithForest rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :SampledCluster ;
                   skos:definition "a cluster contains at least one plot main area with a forest plot subarea wich was sampled"@en ;
                   skos:prefLabel "aufgenommen mit Wald"@de ,
                                  "muestreado con bosque"@es ,
                                  "sampled with forest"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#SamplingStatus
:SamplingStatus rdf:type owl:Class ;
                owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty :isSamplingStatusOf ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom :PlotMainArea
                                    ] ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :PlotMainAreaClassification ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                skos:definition "a cluster area set which contains  at least one plot main area which was sampled"@en ,
                                "classification of a plot main area on if it was sampled or not. If negative also gives the reason."@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "Erfassungszustand einer Plot-Hauptfläche"@de ,
                               "aufgenommen"@de ,
                               "estado de muestreo de un areá principal de parcela"@es ,
                               "muestreada"@es ,
                               "sampling status of a plot main area"@en ,
                               "sampled" .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Shrub
:Shrub rdf:type owl:Class ;
       rdfs:subClassOf :Plant ;
       rdfs:isDefinedBy "FAO  Forest Resource Assement - Terms and Definitions"@en ;
       rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.fao.org/forest-resources-assessment/en/> ;
       skos:definition "Woody perennial plant, generally more than 0.5 meters and less than 5 meters in height at maturity and without a single main stem and definite crown"@en ;
       skos:note "arbusto"@es ;
       skos:prefLabel "Strauch"@de ,
                      "shrub"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Slope
:Slope rdf:type owl:Class ;
       rdfs:subClassOf :Quantity ;
       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
       rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grade_(slope)> ;
       skos:definition "elevation angle of a terrain surface to the horizontal"@en ;
       skos:prefLabel "Neigung"@de ,
                      "pendiente"@es ,
                      "slope"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#StandSizeClass
:StandSizeClass rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :PlotForestVegetationClassification ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                skos:definition "classification of a forest vegetation according to which diameter class most of its trees belong to."@en ;
                skos:note "The Spanish IFN notes down the three main species present at a plot and classifies those according to dimension. The dimension of the most dominant species is further used in this ontology."@en ;
                skos:prefLabel "Dimensionsklassen"@de ,
                               "estado de diametro"@es ,
                               "stand size class"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#StateOwner
:StateOwner rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :OwnerGroup ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
            skos:definition "an area owned by the state" ;
            skos:prefLabel "propietario estatal"@es ,
                           "staatlicher Eigentümer"@de ,
                           "state owner"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Stratum
:Stratum rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf :DataCollection ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
         skos:definition "a collection of plots whose majority desrcibe entities satisfiyng certain conditions stated by this stratum"@en ;
         skos:note """A plot  'satisfies' a stratum, by the conditions stated by the stratum holding for the entities the plot desrcibes

An NFI can choose to assign plots to  strata in 2 ways: 

1. A plot is  'assigned by condition' if it satisfies the stratum's conditions. 
2. A plot is 'assigned by arae' if the plot is in a map subarea which gets assigned to the stratum area corresponding to this stratum. Usually this assignation takes place by evaluating which stratum the majority of plots located in a subarea satisfy."""@en ;
         skos:prefLabel "Stratum"@de ,
                        "estrato"@es ,
                        "stratum"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#StratumArea
:StratumArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :TotalArea ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             skos:definition "part of a forest area for which the entities like forest community, terrain, etc in most cases satisfy the conditions stated by a stratum"@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Stratumsfläche"@de ,
                            "stratum area"@en ,
                            "área de estrato"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TemplateCluster
:TemplateCluster rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf geo:Feature ,
                                 :InventoryScheme ;
                 skos:definition "Vorlagencluster"@de ,
                                 "a cluster of template plots, which are planned to be visited by the field crew. Has a scheduled location assigned to by an NFI specific procedure, often by a grid or by a random method. The scheduled location is its identity criterium."@en ;
                 skos:note """The NFIs employ enumeration schemes from combinations of columns in the cluster data tables, which also should be unique. They don't serve as identity criterium because they could change in the future, but are used for minting IRIs.  

The US FIA in the table PLOT uses the columns (STATECD, UNITCD, COUNTYCD, PLOT).  Remember that FIA names its clusters as plots. 

The German BWI uses the column cluster_name in the cluster table. 

For the Spanish IFN the crossforest ontology uses a combination of \"Provincia\" and  \"Estadillo\" colums which are used in many tables"""@en ;
                 skos:prefLabel "acopiamiento de patrón"@es ,
                                "template cluster"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TemplatePlot
:TemplatePlot rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf geo:Feature ,
                              :InventoryScheme ;
              skos:definition "A planning entity with location, which should to be visited by the field crew. It's originally scheduled location is implied  by the originally scheduled location of a template cluster and an NFI specific spatial pattern.  The originally scheduled location is its identity criterium."@en ,
                              "Vorlagenplot"@de ,
                              "parcela de patrón"@es ,
                              "template plot"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TemporarilyNonStockedForest
:TemporarilyNonStockedForest rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf :StandSizeClass ;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
                             skos:definition "a vegetation which now does not meet the criteria for forest, but did so in the past and  is expected to do so in the future"@en ;
                             skos:note """this can refer to an empty forest community, eg after a fire. Each plot classified as this has its own empty forest community (because it is an endurant). 

the German NFI and the Spanish IFN classify the plot subarea in this way.  The BWI then includes the corresponding forest community in the weakest dimension class.  

The IFN notes down the three main species present at a plot and classifies those according to dimension. Since there are no species recorded on a plot of temporarily non-stocked forest area, the problem of how to classify their dimension does nor arise.

for the latter it's not clear to the author how the data  some the vegetation (like we do)."""@en ;
                             skos:prefLabel "Blöße"@de ,
                                            "monte arbolado temporalmente sin cobertura"@es ,
                                            "temporarily non-stocked forest"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TemporarilyNonStockedForestArea
:TemporarilyNonStockedForestArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf :ForestArea ;
                                 skos:definition "Blöße"@de ,
                                                 "monte arbolada temporalmente sin cobertura"@es ,
                                                 """part of a total area on which a temporary non forest vegetation is stocking. 

This implies that the vegetation on the area currently does not satisfy the criteria for  a forest vegetation, but did so in the past and is expected to do so in the future."""@en ,
                                                 "temporarily non-stocked forest area"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TemporarilyNonStockedForestPlotSubarea
:TemporarilyNonStockedForestPlotSubarea rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf :ForestPlotSubarea ;
                                        skos:definition "a forest area whose associated vegetation currently does'nt meet criteria for forest vegetation, but did so in the past and is expectet to do so in the future"@en ;
                                        skos:prefLabel "Blöße"@de ,
                                                       "monte arbolada temporalmente sin cobertura"@es ,
                                                       "temporarily non-stocked forest"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TimberStand
:TimberStand rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf :StandSizeClass ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
             skos:definition """For the German BWI and the Spanish IFN the border value is at 20 cm, for the US FIA it lies at 9 in = 22.86 cm for softwoods (conifers) and woodland trees and at 11 in = 27.94 cm for hardwoods

The German BWI and the US FIA use a finer classification, but the Spanish IFN uses this single broad class."""@en ,
                             "a forest community whose vegetation's trees predominantly  have a DBH aboye an NFI specific border value of around 20 cm to 28 cm and satisfy the minimum criteria for forest"@en ;
             skos:prefLabel "Baumholz"@de ,
                            "fustal"@es ,
                            "timber stand"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TimedPosition
:TimedPosition rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf :Position ,
                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                 owl:onProperty :inYear ;
                                 owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer
                               ] ;
               skos:prefLabel "a position that is valid for a timepoint"@en ,
                              "posición temporizada"@es ,
                              "timed position"@en ,
                              "zeitlich festgelegte Position"@de .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TotalArea
:TotalArea rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf :Region ;
           dcterms:description "In the population-sample pattern applied on areas this is a population"@en ;
           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
           skos:definition "A part of the earth surface for which a Forest Inventory wants to make statetments"@en ;
           skos:prefLabel "Gesamtfläche"@de ,
                          "total area"@en ,
                          "área total"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TotalAreaForestVegetation
:TotalAreaForestVegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                           rdfs:subClassOf :TotalAreaVegetation ;
                           skos:definition """part of an vegetation of an total area satisfying NFI-specific criteria.  Includes vegetation that currently doesn't satisfy the forest criteria, but did so in the past and is
expected to do so in the future (temporarily non-stocked forest vegetation). 

A reference definition oriented on the FAO: 
Vegetation  with trees higher than 5 m or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ, such that it stocks on an area of a minimum width of 20 m and a minimum area size of 0.5 ha, having a canopy cover of at least 10 %.  This area cannot include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use."""@en ;
                           skos:note """The criteria for the single NFIs: 

German BWI:  forest trees stocking on an area of at least 0.1 ha with a minimum width of 10 m and stocking on at least 50 % of that area. 

US FIA:  forest trees stocking on an area of at least 1 acre  (~0.4 ha) with a minimum width of 120 feet (36.6 m) and stocking on  or covering at least 10 % of that area.

Spanish IFN:  forest trees stocking on an area of which they cover at least 10 %.""" ;
                           skos:prefLabel "Waldvegetation"@de ,
                                          "forest vegetation"@en ,
                                          "vegetación del bosque"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TotalAreaTemporaryNonForestVegetation
:TotalAreaTemporaryNonForestVegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf :TotalAreaForestVegetation ;
                                       skos:definition "Vegetation which currently does not satisfy the criteria for forest vegetation, but did so in the past and is expected to do so in the future"@en ;
                                       skos:prefLabel "Vegetation einer Blöße"@de ,
                                                      "temporary non forest vegetation"@en ,
                                                      "vegetación temporalmente non bosque"@es .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TotalAreaVegetation
:TotalAreaVegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                     rdfs:subClassOf :Vegetation ;
                     skos:prefLabel "Vegetation auf einer Gesamtfläche"@de ,
                                    "community of plants found on an total area, including their remains."@en ,
                                    "vegetación de un área total"@es ,
                                    "vegetation on a total area"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Tree
:Tree rdf:type owl:Class ;
      rdfs:subClassOf :Plant ;
      rdfs:isDefinedBy "FAO  Forest Resource Assement - Terms and Definitions"@en ;
      rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.fao.org/forest-resources-assessment/en/> ;
      skos:definition "A woody perennial with a single main stem, or in the case of coppice with several stems, having a more or less definite crown."@en ;
      skos:note "árbol"@es ;
      skos:prefLabel "Baum"@de ,
                     "tree"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#TreeHeight
:TreeHeight rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf :Quantity ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
            rdfs:seeAlso "Tomppo E et al 2010, National Forest Inventories: Pathways for Common Reporting, Appendix" ;
            skos:definition "The height of a tree is the vertical distance between the base point and the highest point of the tree"@en ;
            skos:note """instances are related by ´qudt:hasUnit' to a ´qudt:Unit´, which ´qudt:hasQuantityKind´ ´qudt:Length´. This usually is ´unit:M´, ´unit:CM´, ´unit:FT´, ´unit:YD´ or ´unit:IN´. 

Tomppo et al base point: On level terrain the base point is the point resulting from the intersection  of the stem axis and the ground surface. On sloped terrain and on inclined trees the identification of the base point requires the previous identification of an  an intersection point. This intersection point is the highest point on the cross sectional  area that results from the intersection of the ground surface with the stem. A line through the intersection point and perpendicular to the stem axis yields the base point in these  cases."""@en ;
            skos:prefLabel "Baumhöhe"@de ,
                           "altura de árbol"@es ,
                           "tree height"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#Vegetation
:Vegetation rdf:type owl:Class ;
            rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                              owl:onProperty geo:sfWithin ;
                              owl:someValuesFrom :Region
                            ] ,
                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                              owl:onProperty :inYear ;
                              owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer
                            ] ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi> ;
            skos:broader "bfo : object aggregate (27)"@en ;
            skos:definition "community of plants found in an area, including their remains."@en ;
            skos:prefLabel "Vegetation"@de ,
                           "vegetación"@es ,
                           "vegetation"@en .


###  https://www.easi.uni-bayreuth.de/crossnfi#WaterBody
:WaterBody rdf:type owl:Class ;
